.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The protocol version exchange (RFC 4253 section 4.2).
.PP
Each side sends one line, "SSH\-2.0\-softwareversion SP comments CR LF", before anything else.  foxtrot speaks SSH 2.0 only: a peer that announces protocol version 1.99 (compatible with SSH\-1) or 1.x is refused, and so is a line that does not end in CR LF.
.PP
A server may send other lines of text before its identification line (a client must be ready for that, a server must not be); the parser skips them, up to a fixed limit.  Parsing is incremental in the usual way: the bytes after the identification line belong to the next layer and are left in the buffer.
.SH "TYPES AND CONSTANTS"
.PP
.nf
#define GF_IDENT_MAX 255
.fi
.RS
Longest identification line, counting CR LF (RFC 4253 section 4.2).
.RE
.PP
.nf
#define GF_IDENT_MAX_PREFIX 16384
.fi
.RS
Most bytes of text a client skips before the server's line.
.RE
.PP
.nf
typedef struct gf_ident
{
  uint8_t line[GF_IDENT_MAX + 1];
  size_t len;			/* Bytes of LINE in use.  */
  size_t skipped;		/* Bytes of other lines skipped so far.  */
  int state;
  int allow_prefix;
  size_t software;		/* Offset of the software version.  */
  size_t end;			/* Length of the line without CR LF.  */
} gf_ident;
.fi
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
void \fBgf_ident_init\fP (gf_ident *id, int allow_prefix);
ALLOW_PREFIX is nonzero in a client (the server may send text first).
.TP
int \fBgf_ident_parse\fP (gf_ident *id, const uint8_t **buf, size_t *len);
Consume bytes from *BUF.  Returns GF_OK when the line is complete (*BUF is then just past its LF), GF_NEED_MORE when it is not, GF_ERR_ENCODING for a malformed line and GF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED for a protocol version other than 2.0.  Fails permanently after an error.
.TP
gf_slice \fBgf_ident_string\fP (const gf_ident *id);
The line without its CR LF: "SSH\-2.0\-OpenSSH_9.6 comments".  This is what the key exchange hashes as V_C or V_S.  Valid once parsing is done.
.TP
gf_slice \fBgf_ident_software\fP (const gf_ident *id);
Just the software version and, if any, comments.
.TP
int \fBgf_ident_format\fP (const char *software, const char *comments, uint8_t *out, size_t cap, size_t *outlen);
Write our line, "SSH\-2.0\-" SOFTWARE [SP COMMENTS] CR LF, into OUT.  The software version must be printable US\-ASCII without spaces or hyphens, COMMENTS (may be NULL) printable US\-ASCII.  *OUTLEN includes CR LF.
